  "definitions": {
    "observer": "Read-only callback after each canonical production tick; no extra simulation, mutations or RNG.",
    "shotGroups": "Categories partition attempts. Context/range/quality/pressure rows overlap. Near-six-metre means release within1.5m of the existing curved goal-area boundary; diagnostic region, not an empirical target.",
    "saves": "Non-goal shots with SAVE_CAUGHT/PARRY count saved; goal-after-keeper-touch is retained as a goal and separate keeperTouched fact.",
    "pressureQuality": "0.2 pressure and0.65 quality cuts are descriptive bins aligned with the prior offline reading, not goal-rate targets.",
    "contactEpisodes": "Derived continuous attacker/defender pair opened only by real CONTACT_EXECUTED, closed by actual whistle, control/possession ending or1.6m separation. Engineering grouping, not a claim of a canonical referee episode object.",
    "whistles": "Explicit WHISTLE_RESTART counts contact-rule stops; all FREE_THROW awards separately include technical/passive/restarts. Neither is raw FOUL count.",
    "transition": "Actual observed phase entries; source follows actual ownership/restart facts. Each released transition shot retains progress from gain and real defenders/lanes/numerical context so relabeling can be distinguished from opportunity."
  },
  "experimentPolicy": "Variants change only cloned in-memory actual gameplay attributes or canonical live manager tactics; canonical player files, IDs, CA/PA and pinned input files remain unchanged. Baseline defaults otherwise retain manual manager coaching and normal CPU coaching."
